--- !u!114 &436308603
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 436308601}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 308e3640226ceb346b1cfcac31db9c62, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: '::'
  steps:
  - targets:
    - {fileID: 729869442}
    infoText: Every station has an Emergency Stop within reach of the operator. Near
      the Controller-USB there's an E-Stop that cuts power to the arm immediately
      if something goes wrong while you're at the controls.
    instructionsText: Point at and select the Emergency Stop control near the Controller-USB
      to continue.
    RequiredOccupiedTable: {fileID: 0}
    requiredActionId: 
  - targets:
    - {fileID: 985069602}
    infoText: "The ASRS Storage Unit itself also has its own Emergency Stop, mounted
      on the rack housing \u2014 reachable even if you're standing at the rack instead
      of the controller. Real installations wire every E-Stop together so pressing
      any one of them halts the whole cell."
    instructionsText: Point at and select the Emergency Stop button on the ASRS Storage
      Unit to continue.
    RequiredOccupiedTable: {fileID: 0}
    requiredActionId: 
  - targets:
    - {fileID: 720042980}
    infoText: "This is the pneumatic gripper \u2014 the \"hand\" on the end of the
      robotic arm. It's what actually grabs a template by its handle and carries
      it between the rack and the conveyor."
    instructionsText: Point at and select the pneumatic gripper on the robot arm
      to continue.
    RequiredOccupiedTable: {fileID: 0}
    requiredActionId: 
  - targets:
    - {fileID: 1910548497}
    infoText: "This is the RFID sensor. As a slotted table passes it, the sensor
      reads the table's tag and reports its identity \u2014 that's how the ASRS always
      knows which template is which without a person having to look."
    instructionsText: Point at and select the RFID sensor to continue.
    RequiredOccupiedTable: {fileID: 0}
    requiredActionId: 
  - targets:
    - {fileID: 1688674024}
    infoText: "The SCORBASE software runs on the station laptop \u2014 it's the operator's
      window into the Controller-USB. Nothing else in this lesson works until it's
      powered on."
    instructionsText: Turn on the laptop to continue.
    RequiredOccupiedTable: {fileID: 0}
    requiredActionId: laptop_power_on
  - targets: []
    infoText: "This is the ASRS Controller-USB. It runs the SCORBASE software and
      is what actually drives the ASRS robotic arm \u2014 SCORBASE talks to it over
      USB, and it talks to the arm's motors directly."
    instructionsText: Press the power switch on the Controller-USB to turn it on.
    RequiredOccupiedTable: {fileID: 0}
    requiredActionId: controller_power_on
  - targets: []
    infoText: Before SCORBASE can trust any position, it needs to know exactly where
      every axis actually is. Search Home drives each axis to a known reference point,
      one at a time, so its position becomes trustworthy.
    instructionsText: On the SCORBASE panel, press Search Home and watch each axis
      check off, then Robot.
    RequiredOccupiedTable: {fileID: 0}
    requiredActionId: scorbase_home
  - targets: []
    infoText: With the arm homed, you can now command it to any storage cell by its
      Table ID. This is the same kind of check a real installation runs before trusting
      the ASRS with real parts.
    instructionsText: On the SCORBASE panel, type a storage cell ID (e.g. 010001)
      and press Go.
    RequiredOccupiedTable: {fileID: 0}
    requiredActionId: test_move
  - targets: []
    infoText: "A full test also proves the arm can reach the far side of the rack,
      which requires it to rotate before moving \u2014 exactly like the real ASRS-36x2
      switching sides."
    instructionsText: Now type a cell ID on the far side of the rack (row 7 or higher,
      e.g. 070001) and press Go again.
    RequiredOccupiedTable: {fileID: 0}
    requiredActionId: test_move
  - targets: []
    infoText: 'This is the real material flow: a slotted table rides the conveyor
      into the ASRS station, the RFID sensor identifies it, and the arm stores it
      in an empty cell. Watching it happen end to end is the real test of everything
      you''ve just set up.'
    instructionsText: Load a slotted table/template onto the conveyor belt, and wait
      for the arm to take it from the conveyor and store it in the rack.
    RequiredOccupiedTable: {fileID: 0}
    requiredActionId: conveyor_returned
  infoPanel: {fileID: 493804593}
  nextButton: {fileID: 1223861148}
  completionText: "Nice work \u2014 you've identified the ASRS's safety and handling
    components, brought SCORBASE online, proven the arm can reach the whole rack,
    and watched a template make it all the way from the conveyor into storage."
  onSequenceComplete:
    m_PersistentCalls:
      m_Calls: []
